            <ArticleTitle>Combined hormonal contraception and the risk of venous thromboembolism: a guideline.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0015-0282(16)62847-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2016.09.027</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>While venous thromboembolism (VTE) is rare in young women of reproductive age, combined oral contraceptives increase the risk of VTE. In the patient in whom combined hormonal contraception is appropriate, it is reasonable to use any currently available preparation.</AbstractText>
